---
layout: base.njk
permalink: /index.html
last_updated: 2026-10-20
---
{% from "card.njk" import card %}

<section class="hero">
  <div class="hero-text">
  <h1>{{ site.name }}</h1>
  <p class="hero-pitch">{{ site.pitch }}</p>

  <ul class="btn-row">
    {# Each button appears as a real link once its URL is set in src/_data/site.json. #}
    <li>
      {% if site.links.resume %}
        <a class="btn btn-primary" href="{{ site.links.resume | url }}">Résumé (PDF)</a>
      {% else %}
        <span class="btn btn-todo">Résumé (PDF) — TODO: add URL</span>
      {% endif %}
    </li>
    <li>
      {% if site.links.github %}
        <a class="btn" href="{{ site.links.github }}">GitHub</a>
      {% else %}
        <span class="btn btn-todo">GitHub — TODO: add URL</span>
      {% endif %}
    </li>
    <li>
      {% if site.links.linkedin %}
        <a class="btn" href="{{ site.links.linkedin }}">LinkedIn</a>
      {% else %}
        <span class="btn btn-todo">LinkedIn — TODO: add URL</span>
      {% endif %}
    </li>
    {# Email is intentionally omitted when blank rather than flagged as a TODO:
       LinkedIn is the contact channel and no address is published. #}
    {% if site.links.email %}
      <li><a class="btn" href="{{ site.links.email }}">Email</a></li>
    {% endif %}
  </ul>
  </div>

  <img class="hero-photo" src="{{ '/Images/jason-hero.jpg' | url }}"
       alt="Jason Yin in a blue rain poncho in front of Niagara Falls, with a tour boat on the water behind."
       width="440" height="440" decoding="async">
</section>

<section class="section" aria-labelledby="featured-heading">
  <h2 id="featured-heading">Featured work</h2>
  <p class="section-intro">A few things I've built recently.</p>

  <ul class="card-grid">
    {# Same ordering as the projects index - newest first - so a visitor
       doesn't meet the four featured projects in two different orders. #}
    {% for p in projects | byGroup("featured") | newestFirst %}
      <li>{{ card(p) }}</li>
    {% endfor %}
  </ul>

  <p class="see-all"><a href="{{ '/Projects/' | url }}">See all projects →</a></p>
</section>

<section class="section" aria-labelledby="publications-heading">
  <h2 id="publications-heading">Publications</h2>
  {% set pub = site.publication %}
  <p class="publication">
    “{{ pub.title }},”
    <em>{{ pub.venue }}</em>, {{ pub.pages }} ({{ pub.authorNote }}).
    <a href="{{ pub.doiUrl }}">doi:{{ pub.doi }}</a>
  </p>
</section>

<section class="section about" aria-labelledby="about-heading">
  <div class="about-text">
    <h2 id="about-heading">A bit more</h2>

    <p>
      Most of what I enjoy outside class ends up somewhere on this site — ten years of chasing
      typing speed, a card game I rebuilt from scratch because the friends I met at a summer
      research program wouldn't stop playing it, and a guide site for a game I was briefly
      very good at.
    </p>
    <p>
      Away from a keyboard I read a lot, though at no steady rate — it ranges from one book in
      two months to two in a week, and I keep going back to The Dresden Files. I also run, hike
      whenever I get the chance, and play a lot of games (Root is my favorite board game).
      Competitive programming is technical, but I'd do it either way, so it goes here.
    </p>
  </div>

  <figure class="about-figure">
    <img src="{{ '/Images/cat-cafe.jpg' | url }}"
         alt="Jason sitting at a cat cafe with a small white kitten perched on top of his head, both looking at the camera."
         loading="lazy" decoding="async">
    <figcaption>I'm allergic to most cats. I go anyway.</figcaption>
  </figure>
</section>
